<p>Three Indonesian members of the UN peacekeeping mission in Lebanon were killed in two incidents in southern Lebanon within about 24 hours, as fighting between Israel and Hezbollah intensified and Israel expanded operations in the area. UNIFIL said one peacekeeper died after a projectile exploded at a UN position, and two more were killed when an explosion of unknown origin destroyed their vehicle near Bani Haiyyan; two additional peacekeepers were wounded, including one seriously. The deaths drew swift condemnation from the United Nations and Indonesia, which called for accountability and pushed for a UN meeting on the attacks. Guterres warned that attacks on peacekeepers could amount to war crimes, while Israel&#x27;s military said it had opened an investigation into the incidents. The latest deaths also underline the growing danger for civilians and international personnel in southern Lebanon, where the conflict has already displaced more than one million people and killed about 1,200 in Lebanon since hostilities reignited.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4j9usLIGfRveKfb1NQYNzhCyuLD5b2sX68-8Qu1jgXWsHdhd6P8px-agQhd4ybBnVGDBj_Zv_QQPfzAi1d6_i4O6NES_qQcjT55TCvXZAEP9dNstkEUqVyxaG30dg5_kNbieokhvb2Ts0S-Hep8QtPMpHtWulO6lFKH97Zwt2Jr_INPPAZx40C2RuDQ5WuV02sdSYVDr5VK3jIIjWp2iC3KS8m2t7g' alt='U.N. peacekeepers in southern Lebanon last week.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>First fatalities: Reuters reporting cited by Al-Monitor said the first Indonesian peacekeeper killed overnight was the first UNIFIL member to die since the new Israel-Hezbollah war erupted on March 2.</li><li>Rapid escalation: The two later deaths came a day after the UN secretary-general had already condemned the killing of another peacekeeper, underscoring how quickly the danger to UNIFIL intensified.</li><li>Expanding campaign: Reuters reporting cited by Semafor said an Israeli ground campaign in Lebanon was underway and set to widen, adding to the risk around positions in the south.</li><li>Wider pressure: Reuters reporting cited by Semafor said Lebanon&#x27;s fragile state and society are being pushed toward breaking point as the war deepens internal sectarian strains.</li></ul><blockquote>Attacks on peacekeepers are grave violations of international humanitarian law and may amount to war crimes - Antonio Guterres</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Indonesia: By calling for a UN meeting after the deaths, Indonesia moved quickly to raise the issue through UN channels. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-indonesia-calls-for-un-meeting-after-peacekeeper-deaths/live-76600314'>DW</a>)</li><li>United Nations: Guterres treated the incidents as a matter of possible legal accountability, saying attacks on peacekeepers may amount to war crimes. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-un-peacekeeper-killed-lebanon-israel-strikes/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Israeli military: Israel said it had opened an investigation, focusing its public response on reviewing what happened in the two incidents. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-military-launches-investigation-after-un-peacekeeper-deaths-in-lebanon'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gd20evgp0o'>Two Indonesian UN peacekeepers killed in explosion in Lebanon</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-indonesia-calls-for-un-meeting-after-peacekeeper-deaths/live-76600314'>Iran war: Indonesia calls for UN meeting after peacekeeper deaths</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-un-peacekeeper-killed-lebanon-israel-strikes/'>Three UN peacekeepers killed in southern Lebanon amid Israeli strikes</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/30/world/middleeast/lebanon-un-peacekeepers.html'>Two More U.N. Peacekeepers Are Killed in Southern Lebanon</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/vide